    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vēnātrix</span></b> ,
		īcis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				huntress</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1, 319</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9,
			178</span></i> Heyne.—As adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venatrix dea,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Diana</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 454</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 492</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">called also puella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 80</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 69, 2</span></i>
			.—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venatrix sane optima, non ferarum, sed
					libidinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Virg. 3, 2, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
